1
00:02:57,599 --> 00:03:03,599
What if the slipper didn't fit?

2
00:05:55,199 --> 00:06:01,199
Cinderella III: A Twist in Time is a animation, romance,
family film directed by Frank Nissen.

3
00:08:52,799 --> 00:08:58,799
When Lady Tremaine steals the Fairy Godmother's wand and changes history, it's
up to Cinderella to restore the timeline and reclaim her prince.

4
00:11:50,399 --> 00:11:56,399
Cinderella (voice), played by Jennifer Hale.

5
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Prince Charming (voice), played by Christopher Daniel Barnes.

6
00:17:45,599 --> 00:17:51,599
Lady Tremaine (voice), played by Susanne Blakeslee.

7
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:49,200
Anastasia (voice), played by Tress MacNeille.

8
00:23:40,799 --> 00:23:46,799
The Fairy Godmother / Drizella (voice), played by Russi Taylor.

9
00:26:38,399 --> 00:26:44,399
The King (voice), played by Andre Stojka.

10
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Cinderella III: A Twist in Time is a 2007 American animated direct-to-video musical fantasy film
produced by DisneyToon Studios and distributed by Buena Vista Home Entertainment.

11
00:32:33,599 --> 00:32:39,599
Directed by Frank Nissen from a screenplay written by Dan Berendsen, Margaret Heidenry, Colleen Ventimilia, and Eddie Guerlain, it is the
third installment in Disney's Cinderella trilogy and a sequel to Cinderella (1950) and Cinderella II: Dreams Come True (2002).

12
00:35:31,199 --> 00:35:37,199
In Cinderella III: A Twist in Time, set one year after the first film, Cinderella struggles with the
effects of a time-reversing spell cast by Lady Tremaine to prevent her from marrying the Prince.

13
00:38:28,799 --> 00:38:34,799
The film's voice cast consists of Jennifer Hale, C.

14
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:32,400
Barnes, Susanne Blakeslee, Tress MacNeille, Russi Taylor, and Andre Stojka, most of whom continue to
replace the 1950 film's cast by reprising their roles from Cinderella II: Dreams Come True.

15
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Cinderella III: A Twist in Time was completed over the
course of two years, from 2004 to 2006.

16
00:47:21,599 --> 00:47:27,599
Inspired by Anastasia's romantic subplot introduced in Dreams Come True, A Twist in Time expands upon her reformation into a more
sympathetic villain, while the writers updated Cinderella and the Prince's personalities to be more appealing to modern audiences.

17
00:50:19,199 --> 00:50:25,199
Although none of Cinderella's original animators were involved in the sequel, the filmmakers
referenced the 1950 film and Disney's Animation Research Library for research and inspiration.

18
00:53:16,799 --> 00:53:22,799
The film was one of Disney's last direct-to-video sequels before
the studio pivoted towards making original content.

19
00:56:14,400 --> 00:56:20,400
A Twist in Time was also the final project produced by DisneyToon Studios Australia, with
Disney dissolving various departments while the film was still in production.

20
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:18,000
Cinderella III: A Twist in Time was released
direct-to-video on February 6, 2007.

21
01:02:09,599 --> 01:02:15,599
Unlike most of Disney's direct-to-video sequels, it received generally positive reviews from critics, who deemed it a vast
improvement over its immediate predecessor and praised the character developments of Cinderella, the Prince, and Anastasia.

22
01:05:07,199 --> 01:05:13,199
Cinderella III: A Twist in Time has grossed nearly
$93 million in home video sales.

23
01:08:04,799 --> 01:08:10,799
The film explores themes of magic, fairy, cartoon, prince, musical.

24
01:11:02,399 --> 01:11:08,399
The tone is emotional.
